## Quickstart

CPU only, no network access, under one minute:

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
python demo.py
```

`demo.py` loads the NeuroTrajectory models of the cross-validation fold that never saw the chosen chemical,
forecasts its trajectory from k measured concentrations, then reveals the held-out wells and scores the
forecast against the same baselines used in the report. Verified on CPU: `python demo.py` runs well under a
minute end to end, interpreter start-up included.

```text
python demo.py --chemical "Deltamethrin" --k 2   # choose a chemical and how many doses are "measured"
python demo.py --list                            # chemicals available in the shipped bundle
```

## Interactive app

A Gradio app over the same shipped bundle, with a forecast-and-reveal panel, a results tab read live from
`results/*.json`, the chip layer, and an about/limits tab. See [`app/README.md`](app/README.md) for the full
walkthrough (tabs, screenshots, deployment to a free Hugging Face Space).

```bash
pip install -r requirements-app.txt
python app/app.py        # http://127.0.0.1:7860
```

