Ingestion and the frozen cohort/splits come first (`scripts/download_brewer.py`, `src/neurotwin/data/*.py`,
which write `freeze_g0.json`, `cohort_freeze.json`, `splits_*.json` and `data_audit_brewer.json`); then run
any script above (each is independent given the frozen inputs; an RTX-class GPU speeds up training, CPU
works); then:

```bash
python scripts/render_docs.py     # fills every template token from results/*.json
python scripts/check_numbers.py   # fails on any number not traced to a result or the allowlist
python scripts/verify_bundle.py   # checks the shipped model bundle against its SHA-256 manifest
python scripts/build_report.py    # rebuilds report/neurochip_twin_v2.pdf
```

### Brewer 4-compartment MEA ingestion

The chip layer (R8) is fitted on the [Brewer hippocampal MEA dataset](https://zenodo.org/records/10257483)
(Dryad, doi:10.5061/dryad.7h44j1013, CC0 1.0): 9 unstimulated and 6 recordings for each HFS condition, each
logical spike train sampled at 25 kHz for 300 seconds.

```powershell
python scripts/download_brewer.py --verify-only
$env:PYTHONPATH = "src"
python -m neurotwin.data.brewer
python -m pytest tests/test_brewer.py -q
```

The downloader verifies every MAT file against `scripts/brewer_sha256sums.txt` and, once fetched, the
converter writes `data/processed/brewer/wells.parquet`, `axons.parquet`, `recordings.csv` and
`results/data_audit_brewer.json` (`.npz` tables if `pyarrow` is unavailable).

